To create a heatmap of correlation coefficients, we can use Vega-Lite's rect mark and encode the x and y positions with the variable names, and the color with the correlation coefficient.

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://vega.github.io/schema/vega-lite/v5.json",
  "mark": "rect",
  "encoding": {
    "x": {
      "field": "var_a",
      "type": "nominal",
      "sort": ["var1", "var2", "var3", "var4", "var5"]
    },
    "y": {
      "field": "var_b",
      "type": "nominal",
      "sort": ["var1", "var2", "var3", "var4", "var5"]
    },
    "color": {
      "field": "corr",
      "type": "quantitative"
    }
  },
  "data": {
    "url": "your_data.csv",
    "format": {
      "type": "csv"
    }
  }
}
```
Please replace "your_data.csv" with the actual URL or path to your CSV file, and adjust the sort order if your variable names are different from "var1" through "var5". 

Also, you might want to add a legend and adjust the color scale to suit your needs. You can do this by adding a "legend" property to the color encoding or a "scale" property with a specific range or scheme.

